`215-228`: _📐 Maintainability & Code Quality_ | _🔵 Trivial_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Duplicate packet-parsing logic vs. Fabric's `toOutputs` helper.**

This handler inlines the same `SyncFabricatorOutputsPacket` → `Output` list construction (parse id, skip on failure, zip with results/states) that Fabric's `LogisticsAutomationClient` already extracts into a `toOutputs(packet)` helper. Keeping this loader-agnostic parsing logic in a shared common-module helper (e.g., a static method on `SyncFabricatorOutputsPacket`) would prevent the two loader implementations from drifting if the packet shape changes.




<details>
<summary>♻️ Suggested shared helper (in common code)</summary>

```java
// e.g. on SyncFabricatorOutputsPacket
public List<FabricatorProcessorComponent.Output> toOutputs() {
    List<FabricatorProcessorComponent.Output> outputs = new ArrayList<>(recipeIds().size());
    for (int i = 0; i < recipeIds().size(); i++) {
        ResourceId id = ResourceId.tryParse(recipeIds().get(i));
        if (id != null) {
            outputs.add(new FabricatorProcessorComponent.Output(id, results().get(i), states().get(i)));
        }
    }
    return outputs;
}
```
Then both Fabric and NeoForge handlers can call `packet.toOutputs()`.
</details>

